{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386359-peach-phengarion-artifact-shamisen","id":1386359,"title":"[PEACH] Phengarion -- artifact shamisen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T05:05:59-07:00","id":1386359,"title":"[PEACH] Phengarion -- artifact shamisen","content":"I made an artifact for our &quot;bard&quot;. Its aesthetics are deeply linked with an actual NPC from our game, who gave it to one of characters as a gift, but I hope it will be readable from wider audiences as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phengarion, Shamisem of Wyld</b>, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement</b>: 4m <br /> <b>Hearthstone slot</b>: 1 <br /> <b>Era</b>: Reign of the Scarlet Empress<br /> <br /> Parasios, the Poet-King, who Wreathes Verses of Mist and Moonlight, the Ruler Between Mirrors arrived to Creation during the invasion following Great Contagion. Here, he was trapped in the strange realm between mirror surfaces, through which savants of the First Age could travel without distance. As all of his kin, he was struggling with the calcifying rigour of the human world, so dreadful to the ever-created and ever-changing denizens of Wyld. In this struggle, Parasios used to rely on the wonder of poetry which can indeed make dreams come true. A great artisan, he crafted an instrument whose perfection would match the boundless swaths of his imagination. <br /> <br /> Phengarion is a shamisen of sublime beauty. Its body is made of a strange material which looks like wood of cherry tree, but resembles smooth seashell in touch, with a subtly irregular geometric inlay of mist and onyx running across its face, its rosette made of gossamer and dream. When the Sun is high, it appears to have no strings, for they are made of pale beams of moonlight.<br /> <br /> Whenever music is performed with Phengarion in moonlit surroundings, 1 non-charm die is added to Performance rolls. Whenever the targeted audience consists of Wyld creatures, persons addicted to the Wyld, takes place in the Wyld, or within dreams of a sentient creature, this becomes 1 non-charm success instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Phengarion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cold Kiss of Parasios</b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 6m<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: Instant <br /> Prerequisites: \u2013 <br /> <br /> The melody of Phengarion carries in it the cold mist of Parasios\u2019 domain. Whoever hears it, sinks in its terror and beauty like a lost wanderer. <br /> <br /> Upon successfully instilling an intimacy by a Performance roll using Phengarion, the player might additionally confer a single target a minor derangement of addiction to the Wyld. The addiction inflicted with this roll will be in effect for several weeks ([10 \u2013 target\u2019s Integrity, if this is relevant]).<br /> <br /> <b>Walking Down the Gossamer Path</b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 2m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Cold Kiss of Parasios <br /> <br /> The denizens of Wyld, feast on human dream and inspiration, born of the world of infinite possibilities. Whoever listens to their unworldly tones, opens a path to their mind and heart. <br /> <br /> Performing a song before a single target who is addicted to Wyld, the artist can roll [Manipulation or Appearance + Occult] against [target\u2019s Resolve]. If the roll was successful, the musician can appear in target\u2019s dreams within the next several weeks, possibly allowing for further social interaction. Generally, the target suffers penalty of -2 to his Guile while in dreams. After such a visit, the player can choose to repeat using this charm, performing a song with Phengarion, paying charm\u2019s cost and rolling the designated dice pool. This can be repeated until the first unsuccessful attempt. <br /> <br /> Every such journey is potentially addictive to the artist. Upon paying such a visit, she has to roll [Wits + Integrity] against the difficulty of [victim\u2019s Essence]. A failed roll results in minor addiction to visiting dreams. Additional failed rolls either strengthen this addiction or the addiction to the Wyld, up to player\u2019s choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Most Refined Prison of Words</b><br /> Cost: 6m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Cold Kiss of Parasios <br /> <br /> When the moonlight strings of Phengarion are struck, one can hear a whisper in their sublime cry. By performing heavily ornamented passages, the artist can bring them to the foreground \u2013 Parasios\u2019 unending attempts to weave the supreme poem. Just like the King Between Mirrors, the listeners become trapped in the obsessive pursue to find the Last Verse, the right cadence to these strophes of unparalleled depth.<br /> <br /> The wielder of Phengarion makes a special decisive attack using [Performance + Manipulation] which affects all sentient foes up to short range whose Resolve is beaten. Instead of dealing damage, it delivers a special poison of compulsion to find the last verse. It has Duration of 5 rounds, Damage 2i per round (B in crash), Penalty \u2013 2. It is opposed by an [Intelligence + Linguistics] roll rather than the usual pool. Multiple uses of this poison stack the intervals, but not the penalties or damage. <br /> <br /> <b>The Dream of Distant Stars</b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 10m, 2xp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Cold Kiss of Parasios<br /> <br /> Opening the hearts of the listeners, the herald of Parasios make them share master\u2019s dream and obsession. They start dreaming of the eerie wonder of Wyld and the Last Verse, the perfected ending of the poem which the King Between Mirrors was weaving his whole existence in Creation, their hearts and minds inspired beyond human notion by the beautiful horror of Wyld. <br /> <br /> The artist rolls [Performance + Wits] against a single target, unmodified by magic and unopposed. The successes are banked and may be used in the same story as non-charm successes in the rolls in pursue to create a perfect piece of art (generally in Linguistics, Craft, and Performance rolls). This charm can be only used once per target during a single story.<br /> <br /> Every time the target is using these banked successes, they must roll [Wits + Integrity] against the difficulty [successes used]. A failed roll results in accepting a minor addiction to Wyld or strengthening addiction to Wyld if it is already in effect. <br /> <br /> Additionally, upon using these successes, the affected character rolls [successes used] dice. The successes in this roll subtract from the character\u2019s Willpower, as his obsessive pursue of beauty prevents any peaceful rest. <br /> <br /> The pieces created with these successes generally tend to have an eerie aura surrounding them. The viewers recognise them as undoubtedly beautiful, but somehow twisted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Symphony of Sounds Never Heard</b><br /> Cost: 2wp, 12m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Most Refined Prison of Words, The Dream of Distant Stars<br /> <br /> As the artist exercises her mastery, she transcends mundane limitations of rhythm and harmony finding the harmonies never heard in the Age of Sorrows. The music of Phengarion opens weak minds to the sublime truths of Parasios. <br /> <br /> Using this charm, the character can attempt to instill Derangement in a single target with a musical performance, using the regular rules for instill actions. In particular, target\u2019s resolve may be modified by appropriate Intimacies. Alternatively, the character may try to strengthen, but not weaken, an existing Derangement. The instilled Derangement has to be connected to context and general message of the performance. The cost of overturning this influence is 2wp (rather than the usual 1wp). <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Opening the Moonlit Passage</b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 12m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Walking Down the Gossamer Path, A Symphony of Sounds Never Heard, Phantom-Conjuring Performance<br /> <br /> When the artist conjures phantoms and distant images with her song, the listener opens his heart and mind so that his dreams and the dreams from behind Creation\u2019s edge are interwoven and dreamland becomes one with Creation.<br /> <br /> When using Phantom-Conjuring Performance, the wielder of Phengarion chooses one listener who is addicted to the Wyld and physically enter his dreams, possibly together with a chosen group of several people. In order to enter the dreams, she rolls [Charisma + Occult] against [target\u2019s Resolve].<br /> <br /> Those who decided to enter dreams disappear at the culmination of the performance along with the phantoms. Now they will be present within the dreams of the target, until they choose to leave them during any time the target is asleep or until they are expelled by other means. If they spend more than a year and a day in target\u2019s dreams, they cannot leave it voluntarily any more. <br /> <br /> The characters using this charm have to make a roll of [Wits + Integrity] at the difficulty [target\u2019s Intelligence]. If the roll fails, they acquire minor Derangement of addiction to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sower of the Cold Mist</b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 16m, 8xp<br /> Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: \u2013 <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Opening the Moonlit Passage<br /> <br /> Reaching the final understanding of the great puzzle of Parasios, the artist performs the ultimate song of distant realms behind the edge of Creation. Hours and hours pass, as from the sophisticated labyrinth of stanzas, crystalline unity emerges, and the long-sought Last Verse is wreathen. <br /> <br /> Culminating a long display of unparalleled musical skill, the wielder of Phengarion creates a bordermarch Wyld zone spanning several miles. Alternatively, she can use this evocation to strengthen the intensity of an already existing zone. When the zone is created, the user may also choose to make a passage between it and the domain of Parasios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}